            "id": "choose-one-protection-and-write-its-limits",
            "title": "Choose one protection you can honor",
            "do": "Name one buyer concern. In the same answer, write the evidence, what the business can control, and the cost limit. Keep unknowns visible. If evidence or costs are unresolved, or the remedy is unaffordable, choose no added protection and say what to check next. Otherwise choose one protection you can honor: a refund without extra eligibility, a remedy with clear eligibility, or payment based on a measured result. Read the draft as a buyer: check what triggers the protection, how it works, and how to request or dispute it. Do not obscure existing rights or promise outcomes. Draft only: do not publish, charge, enroll anyone, or issue a refund.",
